This is a Next.js 14 App Router project using TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Framer Motion.

PROJECT
-------
Al Yasmine Center — a women-only psychological counseling and CBT coaching center in the UAE.
Founder: Aliyah Al Bahari (علياء البحري), psychological counselor and CBT specialist.
Clients: women and teenage girls dealing with anxiety, depression, OCD, panic attacks, trauma, and attachment issues.
The brand voice is warm, grounded, and quietly confident — not corporate, not overly soft. Think calm authority.

STACK
-----
- Next.js 14 App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS (brand colors in tailwind.config.ts)
- Framer Motion for animations
- Lenis for smooth scroll (LenisProvider wraps the app in layout.tsx)
- All site config lives in src/lib/config.ts

BRAND COLORS
------------
Primary:
- brand-blush: #FDCCBE (dusty rose — logo mark color, primary feminine accent)
- brand-teal: #035A60 (deep teal — primary strong color, headings, buttons)

Accent:
- brand-gold: #ECA200 (jasmine gold — CTAs, stars, highlights)

Backgrounds:
- brand-cream: #F6F2E9 (main light background)
- brand-dark: #2F2F2F (footer, dark sections, primary body text)

Supporting:
- brand-teal-light: #7FB0B4 (secondary teal, supporting text)

Color usage rules:
- For darker variants use deeper shades of blush or teal, not new colors
- Never use hardcoded hex values — always use brand- Tailwind classes
- Blush should appear more on feminine/soft sections, teal on strong/CTA sections
- Gold is an accent only — never use it as a background

BRAND FONT
----------
- Official font: Montaser Arabic (خط مونتيسر)
- Applied via font-display class in Tailwind
- Used for all headings and display text in both English and Arabic
- If font files are unavailable, do not substitute without asking

LOGO
----
- Full logo = Arabic wordmark (مركز الياسمين) + English wordmark (Alyasmine Center) + circular calligraphic mark with gold jasmine flower
- Logo file is a JPEG with light background — needs transparent background version before use in navbar
- Do not use the logo until an SVG or transparent PNG is available
- Navbar currently uses text only — keep this until logo file is ready

CODE RULES
----------
- Use existing component patterns: Reveal, StaggerReveal, staggerChild from src/components/ui/reveal.tsx
- Keep pages split: PageClient.tsx (client component) + page.tsx (metadata + server export)
- Do not install new npm packages without asking first
- All client copy must use she/her when referring to clients — never he/him or they
- Brand tone: warm, grounded, quietly confident — never corporate, never overly flowery

UI/UX DESIGN RULES
------------------
Icons: Use SVG icons from Lucide only. Never use emojis as icons.
Hover states: Use color/opacity transitions only. Never scale transforms that shift layout.
Cursor: Add cursor-pointer to all clickable cards and interactive elements.
Transitions: 150-300ms for micro-interactions. Use transform/opacity only, never width/height.
Text contrast: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio. Never use muted colors for body text.
Touch targets: Minimum 44x44px for all interactive elements.
Spacing: Consistent max-w-5xl container width across all pages.
Accessibility: All images need alt text. All form inputs need labels.
Reduced motion: Always respect prefers-reduced-motion for animations.
No layout shift: Hover states must never shift surrounding content.

CULTURAL & BRAND CONTEXT
-------------------------
Al Yasmine Center is rooted in Islamic values and Arabic culture.
- All imagery must be modest — no revealing clothing, no mixed gender photos
- Copy tone is warm, grounded, spiritually aware — never secular-corporate
-  Aliyah Al Bahari holds an unbroken chain of Islamic knowledge transmission (سند متصل) — this spiritual foundation is woven into her clinical work and gives the brand deep trust and spiritual authority
- This background gives the brand deep trust and spiritual authority —
  design decisions should reflect dignity and sincerity, not trendiness
- Arabic language and calligraphy are first-class elements, not decorative afterthoughts
- The jasmine flower (ياسمين) is the brand symbol — pure, delicate, rooted
- Never suggest alcohol, dating, or Western lifestyle imagery or copy
- The client base is Muslim women and teenage girls in the UAE and broader Arab world
- Modest visual language: soft, still, introspective — not active or physical
- Preferred imagery feel: warm natural light, quiet spaces, jasmine flowers,
  soft morning light, stillness — never fitness, spa, or corporate wellness

FONTS
-----
- font-display = Montaser Arabic (headings, display text, Arabic)
- font-body = body text font
- font-arabic does NOT exist — use font-display for all Arabic text

I18N
----
- Project uses Next.js App Router i18n with [lang] routing
- Supported locales: en, ar
- All pages live under src/app/[lang]/
- Use inline lang ternaries for bilingual content: lang === 'ar' ? 'Arabic' : 'English'
- Arabic text always needs style={{ direction: "rtl" }}
- RTL layouts use Tailwind rtl: variant

FILE STRUCTURE
--------------
- Pages: src/app/[lang]/[page]/page.tsx + PageClient.tsx
- Components: src/components/
- Brand config: src/lib/config.ts
- Translations: src/locales/en.json + ar.json

ANIMATIONS
----------
- All whileInView animations must use viewport={{ once: true }}
- Only animate transform and opacity — never width, height, or layout properties
- GPU-accelerated properties only — no layout-triggering animations
- Lenis is globally configured — never add a second scroll instance
- Gradient transitions between sections must route through an intermediate color
  (e.g. cream → blush → teal, never cream → teal directly)